# 🚀 Key Takeaways

- Arrays store elements in contiguous memory.
- They provide constant-time random access.
- Insertions and deletions are expensive because elements need to be shifted.
- Arrays are the foundation of many advanced data structures and algorithms.
- Strong understanding of arrays is essential for coding interviews and competitive programming.
